{
 "about": "What each leveling route was in Grimoire 1.0.6 as first built (data/guide.json at commit e5a5c93, November 14, 2026, before the routes were worked out again to grind less): its hours, its visits (a \"Go to\" and the work done there), its \"Go to\" steps, its changes of continent (`sails`: those not made by the class’s own teleport), its short visits (`thin`: fewer than three quests handed in), its stays on a continent that hand in fewer than three quests (`hops`), its \"kill to the next level\" steps, the levels they add up to (`ground`) and the longest run of levels in a row ground for more than half (`run`), as lib/route-bar.mjs counts them. lib/guide.mjs works a route out by its rules in order (a second look rather than a long grind; quests four levels above and visits of four; the corrected plan alone) and keeps the first that passes `bar` against these counts: no more hours, no more grind steps, no longer run, fewer levels ground (the corrected plan alone: no more), at most `visits` more visits, `thin` more short visits, `continents` more changes of continent and never above `continentsMost` (the class’s own teleports aside: `sails`), `hops` more short stays on a continent (each counted from the released median, `median`, for a route that was under it), and one of Forever’s zones still on the route. A route no rule passes for keeps the steps it had. check-routes.mjs holds every route to the same.",
